From 0fcbb301fb1672d8609d6a2e6ecbe264f0a7f3a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 17:59:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] power: supply: bq2415x: accept CURRENT_MAX in microamps
 from the notifier

bq2415x_update_reported_mode() compares the supplier's CURRENT_MAX against
500 and 1800 as milliamps, but the power supply API reports microamps. A
supplier that follows the API, such as extcon-charger-detect (500000 for a
plain USB source), therefore always read as a 1800 mA dedicated charger and
the input current limit was lifted for every source. Treat values of 10000
and above as microamps.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/bq2415x_charger.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/bq2415x_charger.c b/drivers/power/supply/bq2415x_charger.c
index 35bb0f0e0..509c1c123 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/bq2415x_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/bq2415x_charger.c
@@ -790,6 +790,14 @@ static bool bq2415x_update_reported_mode(struct bq2415x_device *bq, int mA)
 {
 	enum bq2415x_mode mode;
 
+	/*
+	 * POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CURRENT_MAX is in microamps, but this notifier was
+	 * written for suppliers that report milliamps. No real mA value is
+	 * above a few thousand, so anything from 10000 up is microamps.
+	 */
+	if (mA >= 10000)
+		mA /= 1000;
+
 	if (mA == 0)
 		mode = BQ2415X_MODE_OFF;
 	else if (mA < 500)
